# Accidental nested clone of this same repository. Committing it would create
# a broken gitlink, so it is ignored; it is an empty clone and safe to delete.
/eRTMAC-NWIS/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling scratch
.playwright-mcp/

# Large reference PDFs.
#
# ref9_ppac_rr_2025_26.pdf is 32 MB. Git stores binaries forever, so once
# pushed it can only be removed by rewriting history - and Render re-clones
# this repository on every deploy.
#
# Excluding it cannot affect the application. Verified, not assumed:
#
#   * It sits at the repository root, while the Docker build context is
#     nwis/. The builder never sees it, gitignored or not.
#   * The runtime corpus is 248 text files (180 .txt, 61 .csv, 7 .json) and
#     contains no PDF at all.
#   * No PDF library is installed. PyMuPDF and pytesseract are optional
#     extras, commented out in backend/requirements.txt, so ingest/ocr.py's
#     PDF branch is unreachable in the deployed image.
#   * Nothing was extracted from it into the corpus, the database or the
#     model. Its only use is citation [9] in SIH_PPT_Content.md, supporting
#     one sentence of national context on the impact slide.
#
# It is a public PPAC document and the deck already carries the title and a
# live URL, so the citation stands on its own.
#
# To include it anyway:  git add -f ref9_ppac_rr_2025_26.pdf
ref9_ppac_rr_2025_26.pdf
